      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We theoretically demonstrate that Kerr nonlinearity in optical circuits can lead to both resonant four-wave mixing and photon blockade, which can be used for high-yield generation of high-fidelity individual photon pairs with conjugated frequencies. We propose an optical circuit, which, in the optimal pulsed-drive regime, would produce photon pairs at the rate up to 5\u2009×\u2009105\u2009 s -1 (0.5 pairs per pulse) with [Formula: see text] for one of the conjugated frequencies. We show that such a scheme can be utilised to generate colour-entangled photons."},
